# GMS's node is Erda Shower, and the fountain is one of its two halves: the
# player either fires the blast or plants the object. Only the object is built
# here, because past the point a character holds a matrix it is the half they
# use -- the blast is a boss button, and a boss is not what a common node is
# for.
#
# The kill clock is its own: GMS releases the gathered Erda every twelve
# enemies defeated, which makes it a crowd's skill and nothing else's. See
# Skill.kills_per_cast. The 60-second cooldown GMS states is on planting the
# object, not on a release, and the object lives exactly as long -- so it
# stands unbroken and the twelve are the whole rule.
#
# Damage is GMS's 450 + 15x: 465% at level 1 and 900% at 30, four lines on ten
# enemies. GMS turns Shadow Partner into final damage on this skill rather
# than a doubled line; here a skill on its own clock gets no shadow at all,
# which is the engine's blanket rule for everything a character did not swing.
name: "Erda Fountain"
description:
  "Plants an object filled with pure Erda. Erda released by defeated enemies "
  "condenses around it, and enough of it gathered is released at once."
kind: SKILL_KIND_AUTO_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_COMMON skill_order: 11 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_COMMON
max_level: 30
max_enemies: 10
lines: 4
kills_per_cast: 12
base { skill_pct: 4.65 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.15 }
